"Made by the “yellow body” (corpus luteum) left behind after the egg is released. It prepares and holds the womb lining for a possible pregnancy, calms the nervous system and raises your body temperature by about {0}–{1} °C.":"La produce el “cuerpo amarillo” (cuerpo lúteo) que queda tras liberarse el óvulo. Prepara y mantiene el endometrio para un posible embarazo, calma el sistema nervioso y sube tu temperatura corporal unos {0}-{1} °C.",
